      "text": "We use the binomial theorem to expand $(x+y)^6$. From the binomial theorem, we know that the general term in the expansion is $T_{k+1} = C_6^k x^{6-k} y^k$. \n\nIn this question, we are looking for the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term. We want to find the value of $T_{k+1}$ when $6-k = 2$ and $k = 4$. \n\nThus, we get $T_{k+1} = C_6^4 x^{6-4} y^4 = C_6^4 x^2 y^4 = 15 x^2y^4$. \n\nTherefore, the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term in the expansion of $(x+y)^6$ is $\\boxed{15}$.",
